  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145940",
      "title": "What are \"API Routes\"?",
      "lectureOrder": 317,
      "videoOrder": 294,
      "sourceHash": "ec567f27fc1a59ded848b6918e3aeb0ed155c16dfd3b968f4daeafc6ddd5a785",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.26,
          "en": "Now what are API routes?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.26,
          "end": 8.43,
          "en": "It's important to understand and keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.43,
          "end": 11.95,
          "en": "in mind that some websites which we're building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.95,
          "end": 16.88,
          "en": "don't just need HTML pages that are being served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.88,
          "end": 19.708,
          "en": "back to visitors upon requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.708,
          "end": 22.927,
          "en": "That of course is something which most websites need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.927,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "but it's not the only thing that can be needed by a website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 29.88,
          "en": "You might, for example, have a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.88,
          "end": 33.916,
          "en": "on your website that allows users to submit feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.916,
          "end": 36.548,
          "en": "or sign up for a newsletter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.548,
          "end": 39.58,
          "en": "Now, when a user clicks such a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.58,
          "end": 42.564,
          "en": "to for example sign up for a newsletter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.564,
          "end": 47.4,
          "en": "you don't necessarily want to show a different page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "I mean you could show a confirmation page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "that it was successful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 56.12,
          "en": "but you could also just show a little info pop-up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.12,
          "end": 59.36,
          "en": "or a banner on the existing page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.36,
          "end": 61.9,
          "en": "But even if we ignore what we show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.9,
          "end": 64.7,
          "en": "let's think about what happens behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.7,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "when we sign up for a newsletter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 72.07,
          "en": "Then we need to send data to some server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.07,
          "end": 76.12,
          "en": "to some computer to then store that entered newsletter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.12,
          "end": 79,
          "en": "email address in some database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79,
          "end": 81.41,
          "en": "And that request which is being sent there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.41,
          "end": 84.07,
          "en": "is not about fetching a site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.07,
          "end": 86.34,
          "en": "It is about storing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.34,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "So it's kind of the other direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 92.28999999999999,
          "en": "We don't want to get a HTML page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.28999999999999,
          "end": 96.11,
          "en": "Instead. We want to send that user entered data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.11,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "to some database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 101.21000000000001,
          "en": "And that is what we use APIs for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.52000000000001,
          "en": "Application Programming Interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.52000000000001,
          "end": 107.33,
          "en": "There are different kinds of APIs we could build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.33,
          "end": 111.69,
          "en": "REST APIs are the most popular form of APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 115.05,
          "en": "And the idea is always the same that we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.05,
          "end": 119.50999999999999,
          "en": "a web server that exposes certain URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.50999999999999,
          "end": 122.41,
          "en": "Just as we did it thus far in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.41,
          "end": 126.315,
          "en": "but those you are URLs are not about getting requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.315,
          "end": 128.936,
          "en": "and sending back HTML data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.936,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "but they are about accepting some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 133.92,
          "en": "and then sending back responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 138.65,
          "en": "with any kind of data, not necessarily HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.65,
          "end": 142.52,
          "en": "Specifically JSON, JavaScript Object Notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.52,
          "end": 146.253,
          "en": "would be the most common format for exchanging such data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.16,
          "end": 152.12,
          "en": "So API routes are special kind of you are URLs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.12,
          "end": 155.82999999999998,
          "en": "which you can add to your Next.js application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.82999999999998,
          "end": 159.64,
          "en": "which are not about getting a standard browser request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.64,
          "end": 163.07,
          "en": "and sending back a pre-rendered HTML page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.07,
          "end": 166.69,
          "en": "but which are instead about getting data, using data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.69,
          "end": 169.37,
          "en": "maybe storing data in some database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.37,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "and sending back data in any form of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 177.219,
          "en": "So in the end API routes, this Next.js feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.219,
          "end": 181.6,
          "en": "is a feature that allows us to build a API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.6,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "a REST API if you will, as part of our Next.js app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.25,
          "end": 191.234,
          "en": "And it would, for example, allow us to support URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.234,
          "end": 196.234,
          "en": "or PRURLs after our domain, like this /apifeedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.269,
          "end": 201.269,
          "en": "and then accepting different kinds of HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 206.36,
          "en": "Not just get requests as all our page routes did thus far",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 212.24,
          "en": "but also post or put or delete requests, whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 212.24,
          "end": 216.01,
          "en": "And then depending on which HTTP method was used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 216.01,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "for which path, different actions could be triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 222.812,
          "en": "If, for example, for a post request send to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 222.812,
          "end": 227.45,
          "en": "/api/feedback, we might expect some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 227.45,
          "end": 230.221,
          "en": "to be sent along with that incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 230.221,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "some feedback data entered by a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "And then when that request hits our API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 239.517,
          "en": "we extract that data from the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 239.517,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "and store it in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 245.66,
          "en": "If the get request reaches that same URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 245.66,
          "end": 248.65,
          "en": "we instead might want to fetch data from a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.65,
          "end": 253.3,
          "en": "and send that back but not as an HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 253.3,
          "end": 257.623,
          "en": "but instead as raw data in that JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 258.78,
          "end": 263.78,
          "en": "And those API routes, therefore don't exist to be entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 264.05,
          "end": 269.05,
          "en": "in the URL typically, but instead to be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 269.097,
          "end": 273.43,
          "en": "via JavaScript code, via Ajax requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 273.43,
          "end": 276.18,
          "en": "So we as a developer add certain code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 276.18,
          "end": 280.68,
          "en": "to our page that sends these behind the scenes requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 280.68,
          "end": 285.68,
          "en": "you could say to our API to store or fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 285.866,
          "end": 288.74,
          "en": "And that is actually something we already did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 288.74,
          "end": 289.86,
          "en": "in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 289.86,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "When we worked with Firebase, when we sent requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 298.73,
          "en": "to Firebase, then there, we talked to the Firebase API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 300.29,
          "end": 303.01,
          "en": "We sent requests to certain URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 303.01,
          "end": 306.17,
          "en": "for restoring data and for getting data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 306.17,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "And these URLs. These Firebase URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 312.7,
          "en": "We didn't enter them into browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 312.7,
          "end": 317.01,
          "en": "Instead we send requests through our JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 317.01,
          "end": 319.17,
          "en": "No matter if that code then runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 319.17,
          "end": 321.62,
          "en": "on the client or on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 321.62,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "we talked to that Firebase API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 329.23,
          "en": "And now it is API routes' feature is about letting us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 329.23,
          "end": 332.62,
          "en": "to find our own API end points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 332.62,
          "end": 335.89300000000003,
          "en": "as part of our Next.js application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
